# Data conversion between megabyte and tebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between megabyte and tebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1MB to 0.0000TiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5MB yields 0.0000TiB; backward, converting 1TiB to 1099511.6277MB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5TiB yields 1649267.4416MB. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1MB
print(forward_whole->to(TiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MB
print(forward_fractional->to(TiB))
backward_whole: int = 1TiB
print(backward_whole->to(MB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TiB
print(backward_fractional->to(MB))

<<< stdout
0.0000TiB
0.0000TiB
1099511.6277MB
1649267.4416MB

<<< stderr
